# Every text file is checked out with LF on every platform. Git for Windows
# otherwise converts text files to CRLF on checkout (core.autocrlf=true). A
# bundled Lambda's source map embeds its source text, and its asset hash is
# taken from the bundle, so a CRLF checkout gives the same code a different hash:
# each deploy from the other operating system would update the Lambda for nothing.
# Files copied into Linux images need LF too.
* text=auto eol=lf
